The paper’s source is available locally now. Its main theorem is a complete classification, so the prior “choose a known APN construction and ask whether it is APN” would be disqualified: the answer is a direct theorem lookup (and APN checking itself is exhaustive derivative enumeration). I’m examining the paper’s native equivalence action instead—whether recovering a hidden \(\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb F_{2^\ell})\) equivalence yields a finite exact matrix witness with a genuine compact-vs-mechanical gap.
