+
+inst = make_instance(seed=123, **DIFFICULTY["easy"])
+print(render(inst))
+ok, reason = verify(inst, inst["answer"])
+assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After OpenRouter access is restored, rerun the bare loop here and the structural
+and placebo loops in separate scratch directories. Once it reports
+`hardened`, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 2206.00958 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The family exercises the Hilbert–90 engine used by the paper, not the full APN
+classification theorem. It becomes easy as soon as the repeated rank-one row
+discrepancy is recognized; that is intentional for Track B. The random-guess
+density is uniform over all fixed-width normalized field elements and says
+nothing about a solver with structural priors. Gaussian elimination makes the
+family trivial with tools. I did not test Wiedemann-style sparse linear algebra,
+SAT/SMT encodings, or a learned rank-one detector; those can only strengthen the
+statement that tools solve it. Most importantly, the mandatory multi-vendor
+no-tool test did not run because the external key was exhausted. Until it does,
+the local attack panel supports correctness and construction hygiene but not the
+required model-hardness claim.
