  1160	permutes $\ProjectiveLine(\LL)$ if and only if $c \in \f{2}$ and $d = 1$.
  1161	\item If $l$ is even and $f(x,1) = 0 = g(x,1)$ does not hold for $x \in \PLL$, 
  1162	then the fractional projective map
  1163	\[
  1164	x \mapsto f(x,1)/g(x,1) 
  1165	\]
  1166	permutes $\ProjectiveLine(\LL)$ if and only if $(f,g) \GLEQ G_{q+1}$ or $(f,g) \GLEQ G_{q+r}$.
  1167	\end{itemize}
  1168	\end{lemma}
  1169	
  1170	Note that in the even case $G_{q+1}$ and $G_{q+r}$ are APN, since
  1171	$\Gcd(k,l) = \Gcd(k,2l) = \Gcd(k+l,2l) = 1$ by \cite{gold} which
  1172	states that $G_{2^i+1}$ is APN over $\f{2^n}$ if and only if $\Gcd(i,n)=1$. 
